The question is about PHP closures (anonymous functions) and whether they automatically see variables from the outer scope without the `use` keyword.

In PHP, closures (anonymous functions) do NOT automatically have access to variables from the outer scope. You need to use the `use` keyword to import variables from the enclosing scope into the closure.

For example:
```php
$x = 10;
$fn = function() {
    echo $x; // This will be null/undefined, not 10
};
```

vs.

```php
$x = 10;
$fn = function() use ($x) {
    echo $x; // This will be 10
};
```

So the statement "An anonymous function without use sees variables from the outer scope" is FALSE.

